From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:28:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 112/120] stats: log the GitHub stars daily and chart them in
 the README

A scheduled workflow (daily, or by hand) runs .github/scripts/stars.py,
standard library only, and commits to an orphan `stats` branch, so the
log never adds commits to master nor starts a build:
- stars.csv: stars, forks, watchers and open issues per day of Nimbus
  Backup, upstream (tizbac), mjb-is, CJInvent and any fork of upstream
  or ours that has a star;
- stars.svg: our stars over time, from the date of each star;
- stars-compare.svg: upstream and the forks. GitHub lists who starred a
  repository, and when, to its maintainers only, so those curves are
  built from the daily log and start today.

The README (EN and FR) shows our chart and links the comparison and
the log.
